[index] – Accesses a character at a specific position in a string.
len() – Returns the length of the string.
in – Checks if a substring is present in a string.
[start:end] – Returns a slice of the string (end index not included).
[:end] – Returns characters from the beginning to end.
[start:] – Returns characters from start to the end.
[-start:-end] – Slices the string using negative indexing.

Methods:
    upper() – Converts all letters to uppercase.
    lower() – Converts all letters to lowercase.
    strip() – Removes whitespace from the beginning and end of the string.
    replace(old, new) – Replaces all occurrences of one substring with another.
    split(separator) – Splits the string into a list using the specified separator.
    Other Syntax
    + – Concatenates (joins) strings.
    f"..." – Creates an f-string to insert variables into a string.
    {value:.2f} – Formats a number to 2 decimal places in an f-string.

Escape Characters:
    \" – Double quote.
    \' – Single quote.
    \\ – Backslash.
    \n – New line.
    \r – Carriage return.
    \t – Tab.
    \b – Backspace.